this is lucy james reading for ben janka  a new adventure awaits the warriors of  light in end walker the latest expansion  for square enix's popular mmo final  fantasy 14. not only is end walker  wrapping up a huge intricate story that  spans over 10 years but it's also  bringing us two new jobs as well as the  male vieira and a ton of new content on  top oh and there's also a whole moon to  explore end walker launches on december  7th officially or on the third if you  pre-ordered for early access on both  playstation 4 and 5 as well as pc steam  and mac to prepare you for it we thought  we would gather up everything you need  to know about the new expansion before  it arrives  the big thing here is that final fantasy  xiv director naoki yoshida and his  dedicated team have put in the extra  work to ensure that the conclusion of  the heidelin and zodiac saga is  fittingly epic the story started all the  way back with the long wiped out 1.0  version of the game and has lasted for a  decade and this narrative is the game's  strongest selling point for those eager  for story content we know so far that  end walker is the biggest expansion yet  in terms of story and cut scenes in fact  it apparently has so much story content  it gives most single-player rpgs a run  for their money as far as what the story  is going to contain we only have a few  details as the dev team likes to keep  details close to their chest until the  game releases we know we are finally  going to locations fans have been very  excited to see old charlie vavnir and  garlimold and of course the moon as  exciting as the trip to the moon is we  still don't know exactly why or how we  get there but that doesn't mean we are  any less excited for it  while almost everything in final fantasy  xiv is built off of or around the story  there is still a lot more content to do  alongside the normal story progression  dungeons or raids a big one is the new  island sanctuaries mode which works sort  of like an animal crossing or harvest  moon game from what we can tell  apparently it also lets players build  out a home or other buildings on their  own private island outside of an initial  somewhat vague announcement most info  for this mode has been from various  interviews so in many ways square enix  is keeping details for that close to its  chest too although island sanctuaries is  coming in a later patch we won't have to  wait long but what we do have now is a  very nice bit of promotional art that  features the major general so it's  already one of the best things you'll  see another big set of changes are  coming to pvp courtesy of a free season  pass setup for progression as long as  you play pvp you'll be earning rewards  like mounts and gear which is a great  way to reduce fear of missing out for  players who may want some of the pvp  rewards but would prefer to just grind  it out instead of sweat it out in combat  to be in the top 100 players for a whole  server square enix mentioned possibly  bringing back old season rewards as well  so i'm holding out hope i can still get  my hands on that sweet season 19 armor i  missed additionally a new small scale  map for pvp that looks similar to a  payload map in overwatch is also on the  way it's 5 on 5 with no class  restrictions so it's sure to be an  interesting competitive time  with every expansion there is always  excitement about what new jobs will be  added for everyone to play this time  around we are getting a new physical  melee dps in the form of the reaper and  a shield based healer in the form of the  sage if you want to read or hear more  about them specifically or check out  some of the changes coming to other jobs  we do have a preview up on gamespot that  you can check out the impressions of  both were very favorable with sage  getting me excited to try healing even  as a tank main and reaper shaping up to  be my new favorite dps job both new jobs  do a great job of showing how much the  game has progressed stylistically and  mechanically with its jobs a lot of  skills are also being shuffled around  and every existing job gets to look  forward to new skills from level 80 to  90. some jobs like the summoner and monk  are getting bigger overhauls which all  seemed great during the preview event  the summoner's changes give it great  identity now that it actually summons  huge bosses and it feels even better to  play being the tank player that i am i  also really enjoyed the changes to  warrior and even paladin less fell  cleaves will always leave me sad but  that new overhead smash ability along  with the new punching one are already  making up for it who isn't excited about  paladins just getting tons of huge  swords to throw around now too  basically almost every job has something  exciting to look forward to and that's  always one of the coolest parts of a new  expansion  i know there are people out there that i  need to mention this specifically for as  people love their bunny boys people kept  asking and now they will receive and  walker finally brings male vieira into  final fantasy for the first time and i  am pretty sure it's going to change  eorzea as we know it say goodbye to all  your tall ellis and men and pointy-eared  catboys everyone who afks in limsa la  minsa is about to fantasia into a bunny  boy and there is no going back i love my  big dumber garden too much to change  myself but i am stoked to see everyone  else live their best lives that's all i  really have to say about mel vieira  we're all happy they're  here with the release of the next  expansion one of the big things that  everyone was hoping for was data center  travel or the ability to visit and play  with your friends no matter what server  they're on with end walker we are  finally getting just that the health of  an mmo is tied to its community and  having server and data center barriers  broken down means that the community  will be able to connect and thrive in  completely new and fun ways beyond  having a larger pool of pals to run  dungeons or raids with it also opens up  the avenue for visiting and seeing a lot  of really cool player driven content now  you'll be able to visit fully  functioning in-game nightclubs and  listen to live djs play music to full  concerts put on by bards or even plays  regardless of if they're happening on  your server or not personally there is  this player run aquarium that i have  always wanted to visit but it was on  another data center and now i can  finally go this is only going to be made  even better with the new housing  district players came together to build  in ishgard this means there will be tons  of new housing opportunities and new  places to visit once everyone gets  situated getting housing in final  fantasy 14 is no easy task but at least  this time there will be a lottery system  for players to get a better chance of  landing one however it shakes out i am  very excited to see what new places  people make to visit whether that's a  cute little coffee shop to hang out with  other people in or a massive concert  hall to serve as a venue for musical  performances with all this new stuff to  see a new level cap of 90 to get to and  new jobs to experience end walker is  shaping up to be a major content drop  for final fantasy 14. even if we don't  have specifics for a lot of what is  being introduced yet we have a good  grasp of what it all is  the scrapped 1.0 version of the game  around reborn heavensward stormblood and  shadowbringers have all led up to this  expansion and square enix wants it to  hit hard so it's no surprise that the  mystery is being maintained and walker  is going to be in our hands as early as  the 3rd of december when early access  launches so get your friends together  and dust off those swords and staves and  we'll see you there  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

